7592186274905 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186272974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9a0add09-f8b7-5571-85b6-3994fc452dcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186272477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e1f7daa1-80eb-5764-a426-2110070d9e2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186275031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158309" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275459 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute $P(X\\le 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{24}({x}^{2}+1),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93f58db6-2e5f-58ae-a9a5-9aa2f152a653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275459 #edb/ref 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{24}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+x]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}[(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+3)-(\\frac{1}{3}+1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}(12-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot \\frac{32}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275460 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275460 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158310" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275460 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275460 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute $P(X>-3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2},\\, & -6\\le x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275460 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93973542-05ae-5f66-9567-d5a70adf747f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275460 #edb/ref 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>-3) & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{216}{x}^{3}]}_{-3}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{216}[(0)^{3}-(-3)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{216} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275619 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{16}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275619 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275619 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1028c364-ce75-5836-a84c-a7b8c7109998" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275969 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{13}{24}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275969 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275969 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37590d2d-228a-54b7-9ea1-ddb7e5c81f4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276293 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{13}{16}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276293 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276293 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b184341-4aed-5427-a6ea-c4f9d55ff988" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276572 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276572 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276572 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "78b9fe3f-4e98-52de-bbf1-6f4e65819078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277501 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{24}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277501 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277501 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e782edc4-7e83-59f7-a604-01cdc3eef141" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186276293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278040 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b41386b3-26a4-5507-8fde-5cf49c81cb7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278187 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278187 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158443" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278187 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278187 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute $P(0<X\\le 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{3}+1),\\, & -1\\le x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{24}x & 1\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278187 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f2c51ecb-6d65-53cb-ba0b-d70d6940d33b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278187 #edb/ref 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{24}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+x]}_{0}^{1}+{[\\frac{1}{48}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}+1]-[\\frac{1}{4}(0)^{4}+0])+\\frac{1}{48}[{5}^{2}-{1}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{5}{4})+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{16}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419836 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{24}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419836 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419836 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "384b21df-8a7c-5b30-9125-1330da362a5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419837 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{24}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419837 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419837 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3e21377a-680e-57d6-80e2-410c96b326e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419839 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{36}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419839 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419839 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c20cdc4-8968-5346-8c22-76a6ecf55625" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419843 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{11}{36}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419843 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419843 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e2afce84-edf6-5026-8a56-a45c4ffb8701" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419845 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{18}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419845 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419845 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f1943a76-0ce9-5efd-8b74-da642c9f9e88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419852 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d0b9338f-ce76-54a7-9f1b-a16c716aaa54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419853 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419853 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158421" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419853 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419853 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute $P(-1<X<0)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12}({x}^{2}+2),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8} & 1<x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419853 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a05ac3ca-da7d-5bdc-b9ed-2ee65cee279b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419853 #edb/ref 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1<X<0) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{12}({x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+2x]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}([\\frac{1}{3}(0)^{3}+2(0)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}+2(-1)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(0+\\frac{1}{3}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
